{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790009479,"nonce":"TEknXqTD/2pCi2oAipBSu+4ikjA=","title":"Decision: archived issues — orthogonal flag, and a cold set the cache skips","message":"Raised 2026-09-21. Both Jira and Linear can archive an issue, and at company scale most issues are archived — so the question is both modelling and cost.\n\nModelling: archived is NOT a sixth status category. The fixed set (backlog / unstarted / started / completed / canceled) says how work ENDED; archiving says whether it is still worth looking at. You archive a completed issue and a canceled one, and folding them together would lose why it ended. So it is an orthogonal flag.\n\nWhere the flag lives:\n(a) A built-in schema field of a `bool` kind — consistent with status after 5b09ee1, and `bool` is missing from bb9e89e's kind list anyway (a third gap alongside multi-enum and multi-identity). Not configurable per preset: every preset has it.\n(b) Its own entity op (SetArchivedOp), outside the schema, on the grounds that it is about storage behaviour rather than the domain model.\n(c) Derived, no op: archived = ended and untouched for N days. Free and automatic, but not explicit, and Jira/Linear both have an explicit archive that sync would have to represent.\nLeaning (a): explicit because sync needs it, as a field because the machinery is already there.\n\nCost, which is the actual motivation: since 3500366 there is no index at all — the cost is that every excerpt is held in memory and every query walks them. d591cb3 already persists excerpts with the ref hash they were built from, so archived issues can live in a cold segment of the cache file: not loaded by default, not walked by queries, pulled in only when something asks for them. Archiving must never mean deleting — the ops stay in refs and the issue stays readable by id.\n\nNot urgent at 74 issues. The trigger is the first real Jira import, so decide before 33148f2 pulls thousands in.","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1790009479,"nonce":"gwJyGCP+zUPFgA74ya383otdCHo=","key":"type","value":"decision"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1790009479,"nonce":"ImYsIvkdRLdhrW1A7Uux/Deoh4M=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}